# bash-ps0-subshell  (generated by harness/probes.py)
Q: PS0 runs in a subshell; which assignment forms survive to the
   PROMPT_COMMAND that follows?

=== $( ) command substitution ===
code: PS0='$( _LI_T=via_subst )'
terminal tail: ⟦LI-P⟧ PROMPT_COMMAND='printf "result=[%s]\n" "$_LI_T" >&3; unset _LI_T' | ⟦LI-P⟧ unset _LI_T | ⟦LI-P⟧ PS0='$( _LI_T=via_subst )' | ⟦LI-P⟧ echo MARKER-$( | >
=== ${v:=word} plain expansion ===
code: PS0='${_LI_T:=via_default}'
terminal tail: ; unset _LI_T' | ⟦LI-P⟧ unset _LI_T | ⟦LI-P⟧ PS0='$( _LI_T=via_subst )' | ⟦LI-P⟧ echo MARKER-$( | > unset _LI_T | > PS0='${_LI_T:=via_default}' | > echo MARKER-${v:=word} | >
=== assignment inside arithmetic subscript ===
code: PS0='${_LI_D[$((_LI_T:=via_subscript))]}'
terminal tail: KER-$( | > unset _LI_T | > PS0='${_LI_T:=via_default}' | > echo MARKER-${v:=word} | > unset _LI_T | > PS0='${_LI_D[$((_LI_T:=via_subscript))]}' | > echo MARKER-assignment | >

--- FD 3 events ---
result=[]
result=[]
result=[]

CONCLUSION: $( ) and ${v:=...} do NOT persist (the expansion runs in a
subshell); an assignment performed inside an arithmetic subscript DOES,
and produces an empty string so the prompt stays clean. PS0 can therefore
carry a free start tick, but not a start *event*.
